    "created_at": "2026-01-06T00:31:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T00:31:34Z",
    "body": "Let's discuss https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437.\n\nI had thought it was a mostly-CSS issue, so we've discussed it there ([1](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-3160804211), [2](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-3254252906), [3](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-3382444205), [4](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-3666467438)) and also in OpenUI ([5](https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/1279#issuecomment-3309181982), [6](https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/1258#issuecomment-3165384708), [7](https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/1303#issuecomment-3387146488)). By my reading, the technical questions about `::interest-button` (e.g. [this stuff](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-3211111439)) have been discussed and decided, at least roughly. But it [seems](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-3666467438) we're stuck on the Apple objection. That's unfortunate, given that https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437 is intended to be a technical solution to those objections. \n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
